Z||000000||pherder||07-23-2000||06:18 PM||||I took apart my Formula's engine/transaxle assembly and found a mess.  <P>Transaxle is trashed (I have another one)<BR>and <BR>Flywheel is trashed (I will need a new one)<P>What I am looking for is the part number of the flywheel people have been getting to replace the 88 flywheel.<P>If it is:  24576876 (1994 Chevrolet Lumina Z34 with the LH0,3.1L,V6 Engine) then GMPARTSDIRECT.com has it for $55.92 + S/H.<P><P>------------------<BR>Paul, Sedgwick, KS<BR>88 Coupe, 88 Formula, 88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||07-23-2000||06:45 PM||||1988    FLYWHEEL (w/manual trans)  14089201    $167.00<BR>1988    FLYWHEEL (w/auto trans)    14100554     $74.75 <P>From: Scott Backer <P>This is for the 88 2.8 which is internally balanced (no weights on flywheel). If your 3.4 is internally balanced, it will work.<P>Jon <P>------------------<BR>'86 GT 3800<BR>'87 GT<BR>Rossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||07-23-2000||06:51 PM||||After I posted the subject ... I discovered that I used the wrong engine size ... I will be running a 3.1<P>The cost of a replacement 2.8 flywheel is extremely high  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> whereas the 3.1/3.4 flywheel, although heavier, is like half the price as noted above.<P>I just want to make sure to order the correct part number the first time as GMPARTSDIRECT.com isn't very good at getting parts returned to them.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Paul, Sedgwick, KS<BR>88 Coupe, 88 Formula, 88 GT||||reg||11
Z||000003||Cooter||07-23-2000||10:15 PM||||The PN from my flywheel box (94 Lumina w/manual tranny) that I bought for my 3.4 is 10162024 and costed about $100. I will sell it for $100 and ship it to you.||||reg||1
Z||000004||pherder||07-23-2000||10:34 PM||||Cooter,<P>@ <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com," TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com,</A>  I put in Chevy, 94, Lumina, (Coupe, Euro, or Z34), 3.1 or 3.4 engine and get the same part number ... 24576876 which they sell for ~ $64.80 shipped to me.<P>The part number you listed (10162024) goes for $78.11 shipped to me.<P>Don't know what the difference is, if any (except the price).<P><P>------------------<BR>Paul, Sedgwick, KS<BR>88 Coupe, 88 Formula, 88 GT||||reg||1
